# ============================================================
# STEP 6 — POST-TACE HEPATIC-RESERVE STATE
# ============================================================

At the reassessment date calculate:

PRIMARY:
- ALBI continuous
- mALBI grade

Use nearest albumin + bilirubin preferably within:
- ±7 days of scan
fallback:
- ±14 days

Do not use post-decision labs.

Also calculate:

PRE-TACE ALBI:
nearest paired albumin/bilirubin within −30..0 days before TACE.

Then:

`delta_ALBI = reassessment_ALBI - pre_TACE_ALBI`

Define descriptive indicators only:
- ALBI improvement
- stable
- deterioration
- mALBI grade worsening

Do NOT optimize a cutoff against outcomes.

Also record before reassessment:
- new ascites
- paracentesis
- encephalopathy
- variceal bleed
- SBP
- AKI/HRS if available

Child-Pugh:
use only explicit validated class/score when available.
Do NOT use the v12.2 binary reconstructed CP as primary.

Print completeness.

